  ('dde0edb9-48b3-56d0-a319-409e2a01f8cb', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix e- means "out," luc means "light," and the suffix -ate means "to make." What did the biologists do when they helped "elucidate" the mystery?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They proved that the visitors' theories were all correct","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They shared the mystery with visitors from other places","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"They made the mystery clear by explaining its causes","is_correct":true},{"text":"They made the mystery harder to understand","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They made the mystery clear by explaining its causes$q$, $q$To elucidate is to bring something out into the light, or explain it, and the passage follows with the causes: the narrow mouth and the mangrove nutrients. Nothing says the visitors' theories were correct; the biologists replaced guesses with an explanation.$q$, 'draft', 'e3c23a21-e91e-5e9a-bdfa-606154d2af13')
