   $q$The prefix meta- means "change," and morph means "form" or "shape." What is the "metamorphosis" a frog undergoes?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A process in which it heals an injured limb","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-related-idea"},{"text":"A process in which its body changes form","is_correct":true},{"text":"A process in which it learns to hunt for food","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A process in which it moves from one lake to another","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A process in which its body changes form$q$, $q$Meta plus morph means change of form, and the passage lists the changes: "legs sprout, the tail shrinks, and lungs take over." Healing a limb is regeneration, a different process discussed later.$q$, 'draft', '9a26d17e-2591-5be8-b3e2-5287ae4ca605')
